// Title: Change User Account Associated with the FAX Service
// Sigma ID: e3fdf743-f05b-4051-990a-b66919be1743
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-07-17 | Modified: 2022-12-30
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detect change of the user account associated with the FAX service to avoid the escalation
//   problem.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/dottor_morte/status/1544652325570191361
//   - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RiccardoAncarani/talks/master/F-Secure/unorthodox-lateral-movement.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_fax_change_service_user.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey =~ "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet001\\Services\\Fax\\ObjectName" and (not(RegistryValueData contains "NetworkService"))
